1
00:01:31,810 --> 00:01:34,950
[In my prime]

2
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:37,780
[Episode 5]

3
00:01:43,280 --> 00:01:43,710
Si.

4
00:01:45,430 --> 00:01:47,160
Business has been good lately.

5
00:01:47,810 --> 00:01:49,560
They're all parents from the school

6
00:01:49,560 --> 00:01:50,690
coming here to shop.

7
00:01:50,840 --> 00:01:52,400
They even want to pick my brain,

8
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:54,070
asking how I raise my kids.

9
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:56,060
Oh, give me a break.

10
00:01:56,229 --> 00:01:57,310
You're full of it.

11
00:01:59,280 --> 00:01:59,759
Si.

12
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:00,730
Heat this up

13
00:02:00,760 --> 00:02:02,870
for Xin in a bit, okay?

14
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:03,560
Okay.

15
00:02:05,350 --> 00:02:07,210
Qinglian's got quite the temper.

16
00:02:08,110 --> 00:02:08,960
Whoever ends up

17
00:02:08,960 --> 00:02:10,289
as her daughter-in-law

18
00:02:10,430 --> 00:02:11,960
is in for a rough time.

19
00:02:12,870 --> 00:02:13,630
Grandpa,

20
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:14,770
Qi Zhi

21
00:02:14,800 --> 00:02:16,460
is still at the sports school.

22
00:02:16,470 --> 00:02:17,050
Besides,

23
00:02:17,079 --> 00:02:19,270
his goal is to be an Olympic champion.

24
00:02:19,710 --> 00:02:20,640
He's not dating.

25
00:02:20,710 --> 00:02:21,710
He's not dating?

26
00:02:23,870 --> 00:02:25,430
Have you ever taken a good look

27
00:02:25,430 --> 00:02:26,870
at Qi Zhi's face?

28
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:29,360
He has a romantic look in his eyes,

29
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,890
and his cheeks are flushed.

30
00:02:30,960 --> 00:02:32,360
You know what that means?

31
00:02:32,750 --> 00:02:34,610
It means love is in the air for him.

32
00:02:37,630 --> 00:02:39,520
His girlfriend might be someone

33
00:02:40,630 --> 00:02:41,870
we already know.

34
00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:45,079
Romantic look,

35
00:02:45,200 --> 00:02:46,260
flushed cheeks—

36
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,000
maybe that's just

37
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:48,800
from running.

38
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:49,680
Oh, you kid.

39
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:51,240
You still don't believe in fate?

40
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:52,700
You gotta believe in fate.

41
00:02:53,310 --> 00:02:54,400
No, I don't.

42
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:01,310
Si,

43
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:02,530
are you sick?

44
00:03:03,560 --> 00:03:04,820
Why is your face so red?

45
00:03:05,840 --> 00:03:06,310
Well,

46
00:03:07,030 --> 00:03:08,310
it's a bit too hot.

47
00:03:08,590 --> 00:03:10,190
I'm wearing too many layers.

48
00:03:10,470 --> 00:03:10,910
By the way,

49
00:03:10,910 --> 00:03:12,050
I bought you a pair of sneakers.

50
00:03:12,050 --> 00:03:13,750
Try them on later to see if they fit.

51
00:03:13,750 --> 00:03:14,360
No need.

52
00:03:14,880 --> 00:03:16,540
You work so hard to make money.

53
00:03:16,710 --> 00:03:17,910
Take care of yourself.

54
00:03:17,910 --> 00:03:18,520
Don't worry about me.

55
00:03:18,520 --> 00:03:19,840
I have enough shoes.

56
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:21,520
Qi Shi.

57
00:03:21,680 --> 00:03:22,680
Wash the clothes.

58
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:24,310
Si.

59
00:03:24,910 --> 00:03:25,310
Si.

60
00:03:43,470 --> 00:03:45,800
One, two, three.

61
00:03:46,560 --> 00:03:48,150
You can't get this simple chore right.

62
00:03:48,150 --> 00:03:49,350
What are you good for?

63
00:03:49,870 --> 00:03:51,470
Nothing but troublemakers.

64
00:03:53,430 --> 00:03:53,960
Alright.

65
00:03:53,980 --> 00:03:54,910
Look at all these basins of laundry.

66
00:03:54,910 --> 00:03:55,800
Go help her out.

67
00:03:55,870 --> 00:03:56,360
Go on.

68
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:57,310
Just wait.

69
00:03:57,710 --> 00:03:59,600
Her helpers will be out in a minute.

70
00:03:59,600 --> 00:04:00,090
Enough.

71
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,590
You two stop watching TV.

72
00:04:01,710 --> 00:04:02,310
Come out quickly.

73
00:04:02,310 --> 00:04:03,120
Wash all these

74
00:04:03,150 --> 00:04:04,180
piles of clothes.

75
00:04:04,310 --> 00:04:05,370
Get some work done.

76
00:04:07,030 --> 00:04:08,630
You guys are all the same—

77
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,720
nothing but troublemakers.

78
00:04:11,240 --> 00:04:11,910
Look.

79
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:13,260
Here they come.

80
00:04:13,310 --> 00:04:14,190
Impressive.

81
00:04:25,660 --> 00:04:26,210
Dad.

82
00:04:28,500 --> 00:04:28,870
Okay.

83
00:04:35,830 --> 00:04:36,430
Dad.

84
00:04:37,159 --> 00:04:38,920
We already own a washing machine.

85
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:40,510
Mom still makes us wash by hand.

86
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:41,440
What's her deal?

87
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:43,980
You know how

88
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,040
your mom is.

89
00:04:46,310 --> 00:04:47,560
She just wants to save

90
00:04:47,580 --> 00:04:49,380
on water and electricity bills.

91
00:04:49,430 --> 00:04:50,290
Listen you two,

92
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:51,750
don't pour the water away later.

93
00:04:51,750 --> 00:04:53,409
We need it to flush the toilet.

94
00:04:54,480 --> 00:04:55,070
Come on, Dad.

95
00:04:55,070 --> 00:04:56,510
Are we really that desperate?

96
00:04:56,510 --> 00:04:56,990
Do...

97
00:04:58,120 --> 00:04:59,870
What are you gossiping about?

98
00:05:00,390 --> 00:05:02,590
Is it that hard to get you
to do some work?

99
00:05:05,370 --> 00:05:06,570
The Qi family

100
00:05:06,600 --> 00:05:07,930
is really interesting.

101
00:05:08,240 --> 00:05:09,240
Every single day,

102
00:05:09,240 --> 00:05:11,700
they're more entertaining
than skits on TV.

103
00:05:12,310 --> 00:05:13,420
Mrs. Huo

104
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:15,480
is a bit feisty.

105
00:05:16,750 --> 00:05:18,560
Their house is always

106
00:05:19,070 --> 00:05:20,160
noisy and chaotic.

107
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:23,050
But I don't know why,

108
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:25,260
I kind of wish our family

109
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:26,320
could be like that.

110
00:05:40,950 --> 00:05:42,810
Do you remember when we were kids,

111
00:05:42,870 --> 00:05:44,480
Mrs. Huo used to cut our hair?

112
00:05:46,310 --> 00:05:48,510
You were little and couldn't sit still.

113
00:05:49,430 --> 00:05:50,690
Mrs. Huo accidentally

114
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:51,500
shaved a bald spot

115
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:52,830
on the back of your head.

116
00:05:54,850 --> 00:05:56,310
You were so vain back then.

117
00:05:56,870 --> 00:05:57,630
Every day,

118
00:05:57,950 --> 00:05:59,280
you wore a hat to school.

119
00:05:59,310 --> 00:06:00,190
I did not.

120
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,380
You don't even remember that?

121
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:04,650
Mrs. Huo used to

122
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:05,720
braid my hair

123
00:06:05,720 --> 00:06:07,450
in different styles every day.

124
00:06:07,870 --> 00:06:08,600
I've never

125
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,040
met someone so handy.

126
00:06:12,110 --> 00:06:13,440
She was so good to us too.

127
00:06:21,430 --> 00:06:22,040
Cao Xin.

128
00:06:23,430 --> 00:06:23,950
Cao Xin.

129
00:06:24,610 --> 00:06:25,740
Hurry up.

130
00:06:26,240 --> 00:06:27,570
You can finish one more math test paper

131
00:06:27,570 --> 00:06:28,540
before bedtime.

132
00:06:29,630 --> 00:06:30,430
Got it.

133
00:06:33,230 --> 00:06:34,090
Sometimes I wonder

134
00:06:34,090 --> 00:06:35,420
if I'm even his real kid.

135
00:06:36,190 --> 00:06:37,240
Even that mean old landlord

136
00:06:37,240 --> 00:06:38,680
wasn't this strict with his workers.

137
00:06:38,680 --> 00:06:40,040
Since when was a mean old landlord

138
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:41,240
so educated?

139
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:44,120
He even knows pickled veggies
are bad for you

140
00:06:44,120 --> 00:06:45,580
and mess with your memory.

141
00:06:48,070 --> 00:06:49,310
Fine, don't eat it.

142
00:06:49,630 --> 00:06:51,600
I'll buy you spicy strips next time.

143
00:06:51,600 --> 00:06:52,659
Don't let Dad know.

144
00:06:54,560 --> 00:06:55,290
I'm leaving.

145
00:06:55,310 --> 00:06:55,950
Go.

146
00:08:00,510 --> 00:08:01,570
What are you doing?

147
00:08:02,670 --> 00:08:04,070
I noticed your door was left open.

148
00:08:04,070 --> 00:08:05,070
I closed it for you.

149
00:08:05,070 --> 00:08:06,240
None of your business.

150
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:07,190
Mind your own.

151
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:17,900
Mrs. Huo, you're back.

152
00:08:17,900 --> 00:08:19,140
Will you ever stop?

153
00:08:32,750 --> 00:08:33,270
Qi Shi.

154
00:08:42,390 --> 00:08:44,250
You're not done with your chores,

155
00:08:44,390 --> 00:08:45,990
and you have time to watch TV?

156
00:08:47,280 --> 00:08:49,330
I watched it after I finished my chores.

157
00:08:49,330 --> 00:08:50,480
Can vegetables wilt this much

158
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:52,000
in just two hours?

159
00:08:53,080 --> 00:08:54,410
Do you think I'm stupid?

160
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:55,750
You're still way too young

161
00:08:55,750 --> 00:08:56,680
to out‑smart me.

162
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:58,630
No dinner for you tonight!

163
00:08:58,630 --> 00:08:59,670
Fine.

164
00:08:59,840 --> 00:09:01,100
I'm not hungry anyway.

165
00:09:06,390 --> 00:09:08,520
Who wants your lousy pickled veggies?

166
00:09:08,670 --> 00:09:09,930
Who do you think you are?

167
00:09:09,930 --> 00:09:10,910
What are you doing?

168
00:09:10,910 --> 00:09:11,510
Why did you

169
00:09:11,790 --> 00:09:13,390
throw this into their house?

170
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,610
This is outrageous.

171
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,120
We're all neighbors here.

172
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:19,970
Aren't you embarrassed?

173
00:09:19,970 --> 00:09:20,480
Embarrassed?

174
00:09:20,480 --> 00:09:21,810
He shouldn't overstep.

175
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,510
Busybody. Meddler.

176
00:09:24,600 --> 00:09:25,630
All right.

177
00:09:26,120 --> 00:09:27,440
You've thrown it and scolded them.

178
00:09:27,440 --> 00:09:28,240
Let's go back.

179
00:09:33,870 --> 00:09:35,670
She's in her second year of high school,

180
00:09:35,670 --> 00:09:37,670
busy with studies and homework.

181
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:40,310
You should cut her some slack.

182
00:09:40,310 --> 00:09:42,600
When does she have time to watch TV
with all that homework?

183
00:09:42,600 --> 00:09:44,040
If she were just slacking off, fine.

184
00:09:44,040 --> 00:09:45,720
But she's practically colluding

185
00:09:45,720 --> 00:09:47,360
with the Cao family.

186
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:48,750
What nonsense are you talking?

187
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:50,200
Colluding with the Cao family?

188
00:09:50,200 --> 00:09:52,360
You are blowing things out of proportion.

189
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:53,030
All right.

190
00:09:53,330 --> 00:09:53,840
I'm telling you,

191
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:54,690
if you keep spoiling her like this,

192
00:09:54,690 --> 00:09:55,510
she'll never get better.

193
00:09:55,510 --> 00:09:56,240
Who won't get better?

194
00:09:56,240 --> 00:09:56,600
You.

195
00:09:56,790 --> 00:09:57,360
Alright.

196
00:09:57,390 --> 00:09:58,900
Neither of you will have dinner tonight.

197
00:09:58,900 --> 00:09:59,910
Reflect on your actions.

198
00:09:59,910 --> 00:10:01,310
Alright, alright, fine.

199
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,400
Alright, alright.

200
00:10:02,400 --> 00:10:03,000
Go back, go back.

201
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:03,600
Let's go.

202
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:04,140
Break it up.

203
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,270
Help me hang this up.

204
00:10:05,270 --> 00:10:05,600
Okay.

205
00:10:12,320 --> 00:10:13,320
Give it to me.

206
00:10:15,150 --> 00:10:15,930
You still want it?

207
00:10:15,930 --> 00:10:16,570
Yes.

208
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:17,550
It's all dirty.

209
00:10:18,120 --> 00:10:19,120
We can't waste it.

210
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,790
I'll give it to Qi Shi later.

211
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:22,910
Someday, if Qinglian gets angry again,

212
00:10:22,910 --> 00:10:24,110
she'll throw it back.

213
00:10:24,600 --> 00:10:26,080
Do you know what I call this?

214
00:10:26,080 --> 00:10:27,960
A never-ending cycle.

215
00:10:52,320 --> 00:10:52,720
Dad.

216
00:10:53,790 --> 00:10:54,200
Dad.

217
00:11:08,480 --> 00:11:09,030
Look.

218
00:11:11,320 --> 00:11:12,790
Where did this come from?

219
00:11:13,030 --> 00:11:14,120
Qi Zhi just sent it.

220
00:11:14,790 --> 00:11:15,850
He told me to keep it

221
00:11:16,030 --> 00:11:16,760
just in case.

222
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:17,960
I didn't expect it

223
00:11:17,960 --> 00:11:19,290
to come in handy so soon.

224
00:11:20,040 --> 00:11:21,240
We're in this together.

225
00:11:21,240 --> 00:11:22,640
I can't let you go hungry.

226
00:11:22,720 --> 00:11:23,050
Here.

227
00:11:23,510 --> 00:11:23,910
Okay.

228
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,210
Tastes good?

229
00:11:30,750 --> 00:11:31,150
It's delicious.

230
00:11:31,150 --> 00:11:31,790
Slow down.

231
00:11:33,150 --> 00:11:34,150
There's one more.

232
00:11:39,920 --> 00:11:41,520
You're such a good daughter.

233
00:11:42,510 --> 00:11:43,750
I owe you one.

234
00:11:44,360 --> 00:11:45,650
I'll pay you back double later.

235
00:11:45,650 --> 00:11:46,910
Eat as much as you want.

236
00:11:47,750 --> 00:11:49,280
This is pretty hard to open.

237
00:11:50,510 --> 00:11:50,840
Okay.

238
00:11:55,270 --> 00:11:56,270
Slow down.

239
00:11:57,030 --> 00:11:57,870
It's delicious.

240
00:11:57,870 --> 00:11:58,440
Tasty?

241
00:11:59,030 --> 00:12:00,630
This instant noodles tastes

242
00:12:01,510 --> 00:12:02,600
like braised pork.

243
00:12:03,130 --> 00:12:03,670
Dad.

244
00:12:03,870 --> 00:12:05,200
You must be starving.

245
00:12:08,270 --> 00:12:09,200
Easy, easy.

246
00:12:09,670 --> 00:12:10,510
Don't choke.

247
00:12:12,270 --> 00:12:13,270
That hit the spot.

248
00:12:22,120 --> 00:12:23,050
Ah, that's good.

249
00:12:25,270 --> 00:12:25,870
Dad.

250
00:12:26,750 --> 00:12:29,360
We should plan for hard times
in good times, right?

251
00:12:29,360 --> 00:12:31,490
If you eat it all, what about next time?

252
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,460
I can't wait for next time.

253
00:12:33,630 --> 00:12:34,890
I'm starving to death.

254
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:37,390
At your age,

255
00:12:37,570 --> 00:12:39,370
why are you living so miserably?

256
00:12:45,600 --> 00:12:46,330
Don't worry.

257
00:12:47,080 --> 00:12:47,870
From now on,

258
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:49,710
I won't be living like this.

259
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:51,390
Listen,

260
00:12:52,840 --> 00:12:54,510
once my backup arrives,

261
00:12:55,360 --> 00:12:56,030
the two of us

262
00:12:56,200 --> 00:12:57,840
will be eating like kings.

263
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,940
The word ''miserable''

264
00:13:00,120 --> 00:13:01,200
won't apply to me anymore,

265
00:13:01,200 --> 00:13:01,710
got it?

266
00:13:02,200 --> 00:13:02,750
Backup?

267
00:13:03,670 --> 00:13:04,320
Who?

268
00:13:18,260 --> 00:13:19,630
At Hengdong Market,

269
00:13:19,750 --> 00:13:21,720
you can only get rubber bands,

270
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:22,510
soap,

271
00:13:22,750 --> 00:13:24,280
and things like steel wool.

272
00:13:24,750 --> 00:13:26,080
For stuff like silk stockings

273
00:13:26,080 --> 00:13:26,940
and hair clips,

274
00:13:27,150 --> 00:13:28,880
you still have to go through Li.

275
00:13:30,360 --> 00:13:32,360
Aren't they all wholesale markets?

276
00:13:32,390 --> 00:13:33,480
Li charges higher wholesale prices.

277
00:13:33,480 --> 00:13:34,600
But her merchandise

278
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:35,750
is really trendy.

279
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:38,080
Sure, it costs more to stock,

280
00:13:38,440 --> 00:13:40,320
but we can sell it for more too.

281
00:13:41,200 --> 00:13:42,790
You see, every time we

282
00:13:42,790 --> 00:13:43,600
get new stock,

283
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:46,670
it sells out within three or four days.

284
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:47,910
With your taste,

285
00:13:49,030 --> 00:13:51,160
if I weren't here keeping you in check,

286
00:13:51,450 --> 00:13:52,120
you'd be stuck

287
00:13:52,120 --> 00:13:53,750
selling soap and steel wool.

288
00:13:54,630 --> 00:13:56,160
What's wrong with my taste?

289
00:13:56,360 --> 00:13:58,760
If my taste was bad,
would I have picked you?

290
00:14:19,720 --> 00:14:20,440
Aihua,

291
00:14:20,960 --> 00:14:22,620
we're out of salt. Go buy some.

292
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:26,750
Qi Aihua, are you deaf?

293
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:28,000
Aihua is not deaf.

294
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:29,450
He's just not here.

295
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:32,840
Mom.

296
00:14:34,080 --> 00:14:34,600
You...

297
00:14:35,630 --> 00:14:37,450
Why didn't you tell us you were coming?

298
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:38,790
This is my son's home.

299
00:14:39,250 --> 00:14:39,840
Do I

300
00:14:39,870 --> 00:14:40,870
have to report to you

301
00:14:40,870 --> 00:14:41,600
before I come?

302
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:42,000
No.

303
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:43,590
No, that's not what I meant.

304
00:14:43,590 --> 00:14:45,160
Look at all these bags.

305
00:14:45,670 --> 00:14:47,750
We could have picked you up
at the station.

306
00:14:47,750 --> 00:14:49,200
Pick me up?

307
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:51,000
I'm not that precious.

308
00:14:51,980 --> 00:14:53,460
Aihua was just here.

309
00:14:53,480 --> 00:14:55,440
Blink and he's gone.

310
00:14:56,830 --> 00:14:58,080
He's usually so slow,

311
00:14:58,110 --> 00:14:59,710
but today he bolted off fast.

312
00:15:00,390 --> 00:15:00,910
Mom, Mom,

313
00:15:00,910 --> 00:15:02,110
please, come inside.

314
00:15:02,510 --> 00:15:03,170
Let me help.

315
00:15:04,320 --> 00:15:04,720
Okay.

316
00:15:06,600 --> 00:15:07,440
Mom,

317
00:15:07,460 --> 00:15:08,740
what's all this stuff?

318
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:10,080
All these bags.

319
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,160
They're so heavy.

320
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:12,780
Look at you.

321
00:15:13,440 --> 00:15:14,530
You went through all this trouble,

322
00:15:14,530 --> 00:15:15,510
coming all this way

323
00:15:15,510 --> 00:15:16,790
with all these things.

324
00:15:17,200 --> 00:15:18,260
Put them down here.

325
00:15:18,480 --> 00:15:19,510
Sit down and rest.

326
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,260
I'll make you some tea.

327
00:15:21,600 --> 00:15:22,670
I'm not that picky.

328
00:15:25,720 --> 00:15:27,050
Mom, that's cold water.

329
00:15:32,360 --> 00:15:33,490
I'm dying of thirst.

330
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:37,570
What's that smell?

331
00:15:40,750 --> 00:15:41,790
You're cooking.

332
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,530
Why aren't you watching it?

333
00:15:43,550 --> 00:15:44,390
It's burnt.

334
00:15:44,550 --> 00:15:45,440
I forgot, Mom.

335
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,410
You really don't know
how to run a household.

336
00:15:47,410 --> 00:15:48,350
Mom, let me do it.

337
00:15:54,510 --> 00:15:56,240
This is not how you knead dough.

338
00:15:56,480 --> 00:15:59,880
Your hands, dough and bowl
should all end up clean and smooth.

339
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,670
This needs to be wet.

340
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,120
Aihua doesn't like minced ginger.

341
00:16:19,120 --> 00:16:19,910
But without it,

342
00:16:19,910 --> 00:16:21,030
the filling tastes fishy.

343
00:16:21,030 --> 00:16:22,430
Go get some ginger water.

344
00:16:23,960 --> 00:16:24,630
Forget it.

345
00:16:24,970 --> 00:16:25,810
I'll do it.

346
00:16:26,150 --> 00:16:27,750
Teaching you is more tiring.

347
00:16:27,870 --> 00:16:28,530
Go on, shoo.

348
00:16:39,670 --> 00:16:40,150
Mom,

349
00:16:40,840 --> 00:16:42,100
you've worked so hard.

350
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,940
Don't touch anything in the room.

351
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:54,430
You don't know how to do it.

352
00:16:54,450 --> 00:16:55,850
Wait for me to clean it up.

353
00:16:58,520 --> 00:16:59,520
I got it.

354
00:17:13,829 --> 00:17:14,310
Done.

355
00:17:15,030 --> 00:17:15,829
Hurry and eat.

356
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,290
Mom, you eat first.

357
00:17:18,750 --> 00:17:19,880
I ate before I came.

358
00:17:20,310 --> 00:17:21,359
I made this for you.

359
00:17:21,359 --> 00:17:22,290
Go ahead and eat.

360
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:01,140
Why aren't you eating?

361
00:18:02,270 --> 00:18:03,310
Mom, I'm full.

362
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,070
You only ate that little bit,

363
00:18:05,070 --> 00:18:06,330
and you made this much?

364
00:18:06,440 --> 00:18:08,070
Aihua and Qi Shi aren't home.

365
00:18:08,350 --> 00:18:09,880
If you keep wasting food like this,

366
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,280
we'd burn through

367
00:18:11,310 --> 00:18:12,910
every bit of savings we have.

368
00:18:13,550 --> 00:18:15,030
People who waste food

369
00:18:15,310 --> 00:18:16,370
have no blessings.

370
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:19,640
Truly an unlucky soul.

371
00:18:20,240 --> 00:18:21,400
At my age,

372
00:18:21,920 --> 00:18:24,580
I still have to worry about
this family of yours.

373
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:34,600
Aihua, you're back.

374
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,160
I'm back.

375
00:18:38,750 --> 00:18:39,550
Wow, honey,

376
00:18:39,830 --> 00:18:40,780
you were quick today.

377
00:18:40,780 --> 00:18:42,380
Got all this laundry washed.

378
00:18:42,880 --> 00:18:45,040
It wasn't your wife who did it so fast.

379
00:18:45,070 --> 00:18:46,130
It was your mother.

380
00:18:48,070 --> 00:18:48,510
Mom.

381
00:18:49,270 --> 00:18:50,880
My dear, sweet boy!

382
00:18:51,000 --> 00:18:52,880
-Mom.
-I miss you so much.

383
00:18:53,270 --> 00:18:54,470
Mom, why are you here?

384
00:18:55,030 --> 00:18:56,480
-Mom.
-I miss you so much.

385
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:57,270
Mom,

386
00:18:57,750 --> 00:18:59,200
you called last week and said

387
00:18:59,200 --> 00:19:00,440
you'd come in a while.

388
00:19:00,440 --> 00:19:02,160
I didn't expect you to come so soon.

389
00:19:02,160 --> 00:19:03,550
I just missed you.

390
00:19:04,510 --> 00:19:05,030
My good son.

391
00:19:05,030 --> 00:19:06,630
Mom, I've missed you so much.

392
00:19:07,510 --> 00:19:08,070
Aihua,

393
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:09,970
you've gotten thinner.

394
00:19:11,160 --> 00:19:13,070
Your wife obviously isn't
taking proper care of you.

395
00:19:13,070 --> 00:19:14,030
Only your own mother, I,

396
00:19:14,030 --> 00:19:15,360
will look after you right.

397
00:19:15,360 --> 00:19:17,040
No, Mom, I've gained weight.

398
00:19:17,070 --> 00:19:17,960
Look, my wife feeds me well.

399
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:18,920
I've gained weight.

400
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:20,310
I brought you a lot of delicious food.

401
00:19:20,310 --> 00:19:20,960
Great.

402
00:19:21,070 --> 00:19:22,470
I'll fatten you right up.

403
00:19:26,830 --> 00:19:27,200
Here.

404
00:19:27,550 --> 00:19:28,550
This is for Qi Zhi.

405
00:19:32,400 --> 00:19:33,920
Only for your grandson,
not your granddaughter?

406
00:19:33,920 --> 00:19:35,960
Granddaughters will marry
into other families sooner or later.

407
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:37,170
Why waste the money?

408
00:19:38,270 --> 00:19:39,270
Let's go inside.

409
00:19:39,400 --> 00:19:39,930
Let's go.

410
00:19:40,830 --> 00:19:41,790
Come on in.

411
00:19:49,200 --> 00:19:50,160
Mom, I'm home.

412
00:19:53,750 --> 00:19:54,950
Your grandma is here.

413
00:19:55,070 --> 00:19:56,030
It is not for Qi Zhi.

414
00:19:56,030 --> 00:19:57,890
Don't go around talking about it.

415
00:19:58,590 --> 00:19:59,920
Don't take off your wig.

416
00:20:04,240 --> 00:20:04,790
Come on.

417
00:20:06,070 --> 00:20:07,490
This is like New Year's.

418
00:20:12,270 --> 00:20:13,130
Have some more.

419
00:20:14,070 --> 00:20:14,440
Good.

420
00:20:15,110 --> 00:20:15,770
Delicious.

421
00:20:17,790 --> 00:20:18,720
Here, Sweetie.

422
00:20:19,160 --> 00:20:19,880
Eat up.

423
00:20:20,400 --> 00:20:21,600
Have some dumplings.

424
00:20:27,200 --> 00:20:27,750
Mom,

425
00:20:28,030 --> 00:20:29,030
this is the taste.

426
00:20:29,550 --> 00:20:31,350
This is the taste. So delicious.

427
00:20:32,310 --> 00:20:33,830
In the past, our family was poor.

428
00:20:33,830 --> 00:20:35,030
We kids

429
00:20:35,750 --> 00:20:36,640
all grew up eating

430
00:20:36,640 --> 00:20:38,380
the pickles my mom made.

431
00:20:39,070 --> 00:20:40,400
The taste of childhood.

432
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:43,440
Slow down.

433
00:20:43,590 --> 00:20:44,250
Here, here.

434
00:20:44,640 --> 00:20:45,400
Don't worry.

435
00:20:45,490 --> 00:20:46,200
There's plenty.

436
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:46,880
Great.

437
00:20:46,880 --> 00:20:47,960
I am not in a hurry to leave.

438
00:20:47,960 --> 00:20:48,750
I'll stay here

439
00:20:48,750 --> 00:20:50,310
and spend more time with you.

440
00:20:50,310 --> 00:20:50,720
Okay.

441
00:20:53,070 --> 00:20:53,640
By the way,

442
00:20:53,640 --> 00:20:55,310
I also brought two free-range chickens.

443
00:20:55,310 --> 00:20:55,910
When Qi Zhi

444
00:20:56,030 --> 00:20:57,270
is on school break,

445
00:20:57,510 --> 00:20:59,000
have Qinglian cook them.

446
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,160
You're too skinny.

447
00:21:05,710 --> 00:21:06,870
You need to grow.

448
00:21:07,030 --> 00:21:08,270
Eat more pickles.

449
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,550
They go well with rice.

450
00:21:09,550 --> 00:21:10,410
That's enough.

451
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:12,000
Thank you, Grandma. That's enough.

452
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:12,550
Mom.

453
00:21:12,830 --> 00:21:15,310
Qi Shi can't eat pickles.

454
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:16,600
Right.

455
00:21:16,960 --> 00:21:18,030
She can't eat pickles.

456
00:21:18,030 --> 00:21:19,230
Here, give them to me.

457
00:21:19,540 --> 00:21:20,440
I like them.

458
00:21:23,310 --> 00:21:24,200
Your hair…

459
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:25,650
Why is it black now?

460
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:28,550
I bought her a wig.

461
00:21:29,070 --> 00:21:30,330
She wears it to school.

462
00:21:31,550 --> 00:21:33,330
You've been at school all day.

463
00:21:33,350 --> 00:21:34,110
What did you

464
00:21:34,550 --> 00:21:35,750
learn today?

465
00:21:36,550 --> 00:21:37,310
I learned

466
00:21:38,400 --> 00:21:39,590
physics and math.

467
00:21:40,350 --> 00:21:42,160
In physics, we learned about particles.

468
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:42,820
Basically,

469
00:21:43,550 --> 00:21:44,350
large objects

470
00:21:44,680 --> 00:21:46,820
aren't necessarily too big
to be treated as particles.

471
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:47,720
And small objects

472
00:21:47,720 --> 00:21:49,400
aren't necessarily small enough
to be treated as particles.

473
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:50,550
Stationary objects

474
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:53,240
aren't necessarily too still
to be particles.

475
00:21:53,240 --> 00:21:54,070
And rotating objects

476
00:21:54,070 --> 00:21:55,750
aren't necessarily too dynamic
to be particles.

477
00:21:55,750 --> 00:21:56,590
In short,

478
00:21:56,920 --> 00:21:58,200
this frame of reference

479
00:21:58,200 --> 00:21:59,720
is not necessarily stationary.

480
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:01,450
It's assumed to be stationary.

481
00:22:05,310 --> 00:22:05,880
So...

482
00:22:06,400 --> 00:22:07,070
So...

483
00:22:07,440 --> 00:22:08,960
You just have to analyze
each case individually.

484
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:09,830
If you ask me,

485
00:22:10,210 --> 00:22:10,930
all these

486
00:22:10,960 --> 00:22:12,830
fancy theories you learn in school

487
00:22:12,830 --> 00:22:13,890
aren't worth much.

488
00:22:14,090 --> 00:22:15,400
I could teach you something practical.

489
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:16,000
Like what?

490
00:22:16,350 --> 00:22:17,240
On the weekend,

491
00:22:17,480 --> 00:22:19,810
I'll take you to collect scrap cardboard.

492
00:22:20,160 --> 00:22:21,640
Don't look down on scrap cardboard

493
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:22,750
and empty plastic bottles.

494
00:22:22,750 --> 00:22:24,070
Save them up for a while,

495
00:22:24,070 --> 00:22:25,730
and you can make decent money.

496
00:22:31,210 --> 00:22:31,890
Don't laugh

497
00:22:31,920 --> 00:22:33,240
at my little trade.

498
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:34,960
Back when times were tough,

499
00:22:34,960 --> 00:22:36,720
your dad brought home money for the family

500
00:22:36,720 --> 00:22:37,920
by collecting scrap.

501
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:40,230
This is an old‑family skill.

502
00:22:40,230 --> 00:22:41,490
We can't let it die out.

503
00:22:41,640 --> 00:22:43,700
Do I need to learn how to pick up trash?

504
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:46,440
How about this, Grandma.

505
00:22:46,440 --> 00:22:47,680
If I see bottles after school,

506
00:22:47,680 --> 00:22:49,280
I'll bring them back for you.

507
00:22:49,790 --> 00:22:51,920
There's a lot more to it than you think.

508
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:53,030
Besides,

509
00:22:53,720 --> 00:22:55,270
this isn't picking up trash.

510
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:56,790
It's turning waste into treasure.

511
00:22:56,790 --> 00:22:57,920
It's being thrifty.

512
00:22:58,750 --> 00:23:00,210
You've read so many books,

513
00:23:00,550 --> 00:23:02,550
how come you don't understand that?

514
00:23:02,680 --> 00:23:03,160
Mom.

515
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:05,030
She's in her second year
of high school now,

516
00:23:05,030 --> 00:23:06,890
and her studies are very intense.

517
00:23:07,030 --> 00:23:07,680
You should

518
00:23:07,830 --> 00:23:08,640
just let her

519
00:23:08,640 --> 00:23:09,840
focus on her studies.

520
00:23:10,040 --> 00:23:11,410
Studying is important,

521
00:23:11,960 --> 00:23:12,830
but a girl

522
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,440
also needs to learn

523
00:23:14,680 --> 00:23:15,740
household chores.

524
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:17,000
Lazy people

525
00:23:17,160 --> 00:23:18,110
have no luck.

526
00:23:20,790 --> 00:23:22,650
Aihua's been at the stall all day.

527
00:23:23,200 --> 00:23:23,880
In a while,

528
00:23:24,030 --> 00:23:25,720
you go get him a basin of hot water

529
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:26,650
to soak his feet.

530
00:23:26,940 --> 00:23:27,850
Not too hot,

531
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:28,640
not too cold.

532
00:23:28,790 --> 00:23:29,440
You should

533
00:23:29,590 --> 00:23:30,920
test it yourself first.

534
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,590
Here, Aihua.

535
00:23:37,440 --> 00:23:38,900
Okay, Mom, that's enough.

536
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:39,960
Enough.

537
00:23:40,350 --> 00:23:41,270
Eat, have more.

538
00:23:57,000 --> 00:23:57,680
Grandma,

539
00:23:58,630 --> 00:24:00,350
you collected all this just this morning?

540
00:24:00,350 --> 00:24:01,350
You're amazing.

541
00:24:01,820 --> 00:24:03,130
This is nothing.

542
00:24:03,160 --> 00:24:04,310
When I was young,

543
00:24:04,630 --> 00:24:05,490
I could collect

544
00:24:05,490 --> 00:24:06,810
22 pounds a day.

545
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:08,590
Not anymore.

546
00:24:09,270 --> 00:24:11,330
Gotta leave it to you young folks now.

547
00:24:16,310 --> 00:24:16,840
Grandma.

548
00:24:17,750 --> 00:24:18,480
What's this?

549
00:24:19,310 --> 00:24:20,000
A lollipop.

550
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:21,880
This flavor is hard to find.

551
00:24:21,880 --> 00:24:23,540
I don't give it to just anyone.

552
00:24:24,240 --> 00:24:25,840
You're being so thoughtful.

553
00:24:26,350 --> 00:24:27,000
Very nice.

554
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:28,350
Sweet?

555
00:24:30,750 --> 00:24:31,200
Sweet.

556
00:24:33,070 --> 00:24:33,720
Grandma,

557
00:24:35,490 --> 00:24:36,360
does that mean

558
00:24:36,590 --> 00:24:38,990
I don't have to collect cardboard anymore?

559
00:24:40,930 --> 00:24:42,070
So that's why you brought me a lollipop

560
00:24:42,070 --> 00:24:43,030
first thing this morning.

561
00:24:43,030 --> 00:24:44,430
You were buttering me up.

562
00:24:44,440 --> 00:24:46,440
Trying to get out of work at your age?

563
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:48,350
That won't fly.

564
00:24:51,480 --> 00:24:52,310
Lazy people

565
00:24:52,390 --> 00:24:53,200
have no luck.

566
00:24:53,590 --> 00:24:54,790
Don't try to be slick.

567
00:24:54,790 --> 00:24:56,050
You still have to work.

568
00:24:56,510 --> 00:24:56,880
Go,

569
00:24:57,900 --> 00:24:59,700
bring that cardboard over here.

570
00:25:12,510 --> 00:25:13,310
Look at this.

571
00:25:13,510 --> 00:25:14,920
This box was perfectly fine.

572
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:16,400
They threw it away just like that.

573
00:25:16,400 --> 00:25:17,750
But if you tear it apart,

574
00:25:17,960 --> 00:25:18,960
it's worth money.

575
00:25:19,590 --> 00:25:20,070
Take it.

576
00:25:20,830 --> 00:25:21,480
Take it.

577
00:25:22,510 --> 00:25:23,310
This...

578
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:25,240
How much can this sell for?

579
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:26,550
Your vision

580
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:28,070
is just like your mother's.

581
00:25:28,070 --> 00:25:29,790
You only see what's right in front of you.

582
00:25:29,790 --> 00:25:31,310
No one buys single scraps.

583
00:25:31,790 --> 00:25:33,400
You have to sell it by weight.

584
00:25:34,240 --> 00:25:36,000
How much more do we need to collect?

585
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:36,510
What?

586
00:25:36,680 --> 00:25:37,680
Think it's dirty?

587
00:25:37,880 --> 00:25:39,590
If you hate getting dirty,
don't make this money.

588
00:25:39,590 --> 00:25:40,920
Stop being so picky.

589
00:25:41,070 --> 00:25:42,400
You're just spoiled.

590
00:25:43,070 --> 00:25:45,720
You... you don't want this trash,

591
00:25:45,750 --> 00:25:46,150
right?

592
00:25:46,160 --> 00:25:47,620
I'll throw it away for you.

593
00:25:48,070 --> 00:25:49,530
I'll throw it away for you.

594
00:25:51,830 --> 00:25:52,400
Grandma.

595
00:25:53,110 --> 00:25:55,270
Grandma, let's not take it. Let's go.

596
00:25:55,310 --> 00:25:56,200
Why leave?

597
00:25:56,510 --> 00:25:58,040
There's treasure in there.

598
00:25:58,110 --> 00:25:59,680
But look at how she acted.

599
00:25:59,790 --> 00:26:00,510
Acted how?

600
00:26:01,350 --> 00:26:02,950
Did she give you a dirty look?

601
00:26:03,550 --> 00:26:05,160
Just don't look at her.

602
00:26:05,440 --> 00:26:06,920
Keep your head up.

603
00:26:07,160 --> 00:26:09,190
Are you ashamed of making money?

604
00:26:09,400 --> 00:26:10,550
Making money isn't shameful.

605
00:26:10,550 --> 00:26:11,000
But why do we have to

606
00:26:11,000 --> 00:26:12,110
make money by picking up trash?

607
00:26:12,110 --> 00:26:12,640
Sir.

608
00:26:12,880 --> 00:26:13,790
I'll be right back.

609
00:26:13,790 --> 00:26:14,450
Okay, sure.

610
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:15,960
No, no, no. Don't.

611
00:26:15,960 --> 00:26:16,750
Grandma, Grandma.

612
00:26:16,750 --> 00:26:17,750
Let's go, let's go.

613
00:26:17,750 --> 00:26:18,350
Take it.

614
00:26:18,640 --> 00:26:19,570
Take it, take it.

615
00:26:24,000 --> 00:26:26,130
Just one sip left. Are you drinking it?

616
00:26:46,240 --> 00:26:46,790
Come.

617
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:49,480
Qi Shi.

618
00:26:49,920 --> 00:26:50,200
Here.

619
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:51,200
Come, come, come.

620
00:27:00,550 --> 00:27:01,920
What are you doing? It's so noisy.

621
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:03,620
You're top of your class at school,

622
00:27:03,620 --> 00:27:06,280
and you're pretty good at
collecting trash too.

623
00:27:06,640 --> 00:27:07,970
I excel at whatever I do.

624
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,880
Every profession produces its own master.

625
00:27:09,880 --> 00:27:10,550
Got it?

626
00:27:13,070 --> 00:27:13,720
Now that you're back from school,

627
00:27:13,720 --> 00:27:15,440
why are you still wearing the wig?

628
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:16,500
My grandma is here.

629
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:18,340
My mom won't let me take it off.

630
00:27:26,590 --> 00:27:27,460
How much can you sell

631
00:27:27,460 --> 00:27:28,680
these water bottles for?

632
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:29,610
Tell me about it.

633
00:27:30,830 --> 00:27:32,030
My grandmother has been

634
00:27:32,030 --> 00:27:33,290
frugal her whole life.

635
00:27:33,560 --> 00:27:34,440
Her lifestyle is totally

636
00:27:34,440 --> 00:27:35,640
different from ours.

637
00:27:36,040 --> 00:27:37,270
I've got a pile of homework,

638
00:27:37,270 --> 00:27:38,680
and she's dragging me out
to pick up trash.

639
00:27:38,680 --> 00:27:39,030
I mean

640
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:40,310
isn't this just...

641
00:27:40,310 --> 00:27:40,750
Just...

642
00:27:40,750 --> 00:27:42,480
Making trouble out of nothing?

643
00:27:45,440 --> 00:27:46,510
So many bottles.

644
00:27:48,080 --> 00:27:48,640
I don't know

645
00:27:48,640 --> 00:27:50,440
when I'll finish crushing them.

646
00:27:52,190 --> 00:27:53,240
I'll take you somewhere.

647
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:54,240
Bring your stuff.

648
00:27:54,720 --> 00:27:55,350
Where?

649
00:27:56,120 --> 00:27:57,350
You've gotta help me.

650
00:28:01,920 --> 00:28:02,720
Put them here.

651
00:28:05,310 --> 00:28:06,110
What?

652
00:28:08,210 --> 00:28:09,000
What are you doing?

653
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:10,860
I spent all day collecting those.

654
00:28:11,920 --> 00:28:12,980
What are you doing?

655
00:28:13,160 --> 00:28:14,490
Saving you some effort.

656
00:28:14,830 --> 00:28:16,290
How does this save effort?

657
00:28:20,400 --> 00:28:20,830
Hurry.

658
00:28:21,110 --> 00:28:21,880
Stand back.

659
00:28:30,030 --> 00:28:30,890
Not bad, right?

660
00:28:31,200 --> 00:28:32,980
This really saves effort.

661
00:28:33,340 --> 00:28:34,370
This is great.

662
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:41,080
This is much better than stepping on it.

663
00:28:41,310 --> 00:28:41,910
How did you

664
00:28:41,950 --> 00:28:43,400
come up with this idea?

665
00:28:43,590 --> 00:28:44,720
I'm just that smart.

666
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:46,880
Wish you'd put that smarts

667
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:48,570
into your math later.

668
00:28:57,830 --> 00:28:58,360
Alright.

669
00:28:59,000 --> 00:28:59,440
Okay.

670
00:28:59,880 --> 00:29:00,400
This is

671
00:29:03,400 --> 00:29:03,880
for you.

672
00:29:04,920 --> 00:29:06,400
Take it to the recycling station tomorrow.

673
00:29:06,400 --> 00:29:07,790
You can exchange it for a soda.

674
00:29:07,790 --> 00:29:09,050
What are you two doing?

675
00:29:10,510 --> 00:29:11,030
Go, go, go. Don't.

676
00:29:11,030 --> 00:29:11,960
My bottles. My bottles.

677
00:29:11,960 --> 00:29:12,350
Forget the bottles.

678
00:29:12,350 --> 00:29:12,680
No.

679
00:29:12,680 --> 00:29:13,070
Forget the bottles.

680
00:29:13,070 --> 00:29:13,640
My bottles.

681
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:14,680
It's so dangerous.

682
00:29:14,680 --> 00:29:16,510
I worked so hard to collect those.

683
00:29:16,510 --> 00:29:17,590
We'll be in big trouble.

684
00:29:17,590 --> 00:29:18,440
-Quick, quick.
-My bottles.

685
00:29:18,440 --> 00:29:20,100
Cao Xin, I'm not done with you.

686
00:29:26,270 --> 00:29:27,670
We worked all afternoon,

687
00:29:27,680 --> 00:29:29,280
and can't even buy two sodas.

688
00:29:30,030 --> 00:29:31,160
It's all your fault.

689
00:29:39,240 --> 00:29:39,900
One bottle.

690
00:29:41,590 --> 00:29:42,590
Fine, I'll crush bottles

691
00:29:42,590 --> 00:29:43,440
for you every day

692
00:29:43,440 --> 00:29:44,840
to make it up to you. Okay?

693
00:29:45,200 --> 00:29:46,800
Alright, you're not all bad.

694
00:29:53,800 --> 00:29:54,480
I've never felt

695
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:55,850
that soda tasted this good.

696
00:29:55,850 --> 00:29:56,850
Maybe that's why

697
00:29:56,880 --> 00:29:58,720
money you earn with your own two hands

698
00:29:58,720 --> 00:30:00,320
feels especially precious.

699
00:30:01,270 --> 00:30:02,330
Thinking about it,

700
00:30:02,400 --> 00:30:04,510
picking up trash is somewhat meaningful.

701
00:30:04,510 --> 00:30:05,400
You even got a sense of achievement

702
00:30:05,400 --> 00:30:06,660
from picking up trash.

703
00:30:08,080 --> 00:30:10,080
Not exactly a sense of achievement.

704
00:30:10,160 --> 00:30:11,590
Grandma's words are rough,

705
00:30:11,590 --> 00:30:12,990
but she makes good sense.

706
00:30:13,920 --> 00:30:15,440
I mean, at her age,

707
00:30:15,760 --> 00:30:17,890
why would she still bother with this?

708
00:30:17,920 --> 00:30:18,830
What's the point?

709
00:30:18,830 --> 00:30:20,240
She just feels bad for my dad

710
00:30:20,240 --> 00:30:22,040
and wants to help out the family.

711
00:30:22,640 --> 00:30:23,700
Thinking about it,

712
00:30:24,360 --> 00:30:26,160
money earned with your own hands

713
00:30:26,160 --> 00:30:27,220
is never shameful.

714
00:30:27,480 --> 00:30:29,140
Good summary of the main idea.

715
00:30:29,590 --> 00:30:30,790
School's paying off.

716
00:30:31,320 --> 00:30:32,150
But speaking of which,

717
00:30:32,150 --> 00:30:34,210
when is your grandmother going back?

718
00:30:35,050 --> 00:30:36,350
It can't be that every weekend

719
00:30:36,350 --> 00:30:38,210
she drags you out to pick up trash.

720
00:30:41,440 --> 00:30:41,960
Honey.

721
00:30:42,590 --> 00:30:43,190
Come here.

722
00:30:43,410 --> 00:30:44,610
Sit down and try this.

723
00:30:44,990 --> 00:30:46,430
Come, sit here and try it.

724
00:30:47,110 --> 00:30:47,920
Haven't you been complaining

725
00:30:47,920 --> 00:30:49,030
about your backache?

726
00:30:49,030 --> 00:30:49,400
Look,

727
00:30:49,400 --> 00:30:50,570
I bought you a heating pad.

728
00:30:50,570 --> 00:30:51,830
Come, sit down and try it.

729
00:30:51,830 --> 00:30:53,360
It's soft and comfortable.

730
00:30:53,920 --> 00:30:55,030
It's Rainbow brand,

731
00:30:55,030 --> 00:30:56,200
a well-known trademark.

732
00:30:56,200 --> 00:30:57,330
How is it? Is it warm?

733
00:30:58,720 --> 00:30:59,860
Winter is almost over.

734
00:30:59,860 --> 00:31:01,420
Stop trying to flatter me.

735
00:31:01,570 --> 00:31:02,240
Alright,

736
00:31:02,270 --> 00:31:03,400
put it away quickly.

737
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:07,060
Stop wasting money on useless stuff.

738
00:31:07,350 --> 00:31:09,270
If you really want me comfortable,

739
00:31:09,270 --> 00:31:11,070
get your mom to go back home soon.

740
00:31:11,880 --> 00:31:13,280
Mom's been such a big help

741
00:31:13,640 --> 00:31:15,830
around the house since she arrived.

742
00:31:16,350 --> 00:31:17,350
Isn't that great?

743
00:31:18,030 --> 00:31:19,490
Only you think it's great.

744
00:31:20,250 --> 00:31:21,200
Now when I'm at home,

745
00:31:21,200 --> 00:31:22,600
everything I do is wrong.

746
00:31:22,640 --> 00:31:24,370
Qi Shi is having a hard time too.

747
00:31:26,130 --> 00:31:27,170
She's a tall,

748
00:31:27,200 --> 00:31:28,350
teenager girl,

749
00:31:28,690 --> 00:31:30,160
and she's out there every day

750
00:31:30,160 --> 00:31:31,010
picking up trash with your mom.

751
00:31:31,010 --> 00:31:31,640
Tell me,

752
00:31:31,660 --> 00:31:33,120
if her classmates see her,

753
00:31:33,270 --> 00:31:34,550
wouldn't it be embarrassing?

754
00:31:34,550 --> 00:31:36,070
Her fingernails

755
00:31:36,350 --> 00:31:37,310
get all caked

756
00:31:37,310 --> 00:31:38,480
in black grime.

757
00:31:40,240 --> 00:31:41,310
If Cao Dongfang sees her,

758
00:31:41,310 --> 00:31:42,110
he might think

759
00:31:42,160 --> 00:31:43,290
we mistreat our kid.

760
00:31:44,550 --> 00:31:45,000
Okay.

761
00:31:45,440 --> 00:31:46,830
I'll talk to my mom later.

762
00:31:46,830 --> 00:31:47,270
Also,

763
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:48,790
your mom likes to stuff the house

764
00:31:48,790 --> 00:31:50,160
full of hoarded things,

765
00:31:50,440 --> 00:31:51,680
just like a garbage dump.

766
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:52,310
She says

767
00:31:52,680 --> 00:31:54,100
buying in bulk is easier to bargain.

768
00:31:54,100 --> 00:31:55,880
Our place isn't big to begin with.

769
00:31:55,880 --> 00:31:56,310
Right?

770
00:31:56,720 --> 00:31:57,270
Now,

771
00:31:57,750 --> 00:31:58,720
there's barely any room

772
00:31:58,720 --> 00:31:59,510
to even stand.

773
00:31:59,510 --> 00:32:00,750
Alright, honey.

774
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:04,550
I'll figure something out later.

775
00:32:04,550 --> 00:32:06,350
Try to get my mom to go back early.

776
00:32:06,740 --> 00:32:07,470
Okay?

777
00:32:26,350 --> 00:32:27,480
The Cao family

778
00:32:28,200 --> 00:32:29,460
really has no decency.

779
00:32:29,720 --> 00:32:30,920
So many good clothes,

780
00:32:31,920 --> 00:32:32,920
just thrown away.

781
00:32:33,270 --> 00:32:34,930
Just because you've got money

782
00:32:35,070 --> 00:32:37,530
doesn't mean you can
waste things like this.

783
00:32:41,510 --> 00:32:43,240
Remember what you have to say today.

784
00:32:43,240 --> 00:32:45,080
Aihua, how much did you make today?

785
00:32:45,080 --> 00:32:46,740
How much? I'm not telling you.

786
00:32:47,270 --> 00:32:48,310
Remember

787
00:32:48,310 --> 00:32:49,770
what you have to say today.

788
00:32:50,440 --> 00:32:51,550
Don't worry, honey.

789
00:32:51,550 --> 00:32:52,350
I've got this.

790
00:32:54,670 --> 00:32:56,070
Where did all these clothes come from?

791
00:32:56,070 --> 00:32:56,960
Yeah.

792
00:32:57,050 --> 00:32:58,070
Stop, stop, stop.

793
00:32:58,070 --> 00:32:58,510
Stop.

794
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:01,940
This...

795
00:33:05,480 --> 00:33:05,960
This...

796
00:33:06,390 --> 00:33:07,790
These are all old clothes.

797
00:33:07,790 --> 00:33:09,310
Why do they smell so musty?

798
00:33:10,030 --> 00:33:10,920
These clothes look

799
00:33:10,920 --> 00:33:12,350
kind of familiar.

800
00:33:13,830 --> 00:33:15,760
Could these be from the Cao family?

801
00:33:16,640 --> 00:33:17,310
No way.

802
00:33:17,840 --> 00:33:19,240
What do you mean no way? Look.

803
00:33:19,240 --> 00:33:20,510
This is a pair of Cao Xin's old pants.

804
00:33:20,510 --> 00:33:21,770
I patched them myself.

805
00:33:22,480 --> 00:33:23,740
You're back from work.

806
00:33:24,400 --> 00:33:25,070
-Mom.
-Mom.

807
00:33:26,110 --> 00:33:26,640
These clothes—

808
00:33:26,640 --> 00:33:27,830
where did they come from?

809
00:33:27,830 --> 00:33:28,760
I picked them up.

810
00:33:29,030 --> 00:33:30,240
They looked perfectly fine,

811
00:33:30,240 --> 00:33:31,100
so I washed them

812
00:33:31,200 --> 00:33:32,860
and was going to put them away.

813
00:33:33,640 --> 00:33:34,200
Mom.

814
00:33:34,440 --> 00:33:34,880
I mean,

815
00:33:35,110 --> 00:33:35,770
the Cao family

816
00:33:35,770 --> 00:33:37,430
threw these old clothes away,

817
00:33:38,050 --> 00:33:38,880
and you picked them up.

818
00:33:38,880 --> 00:33:40,270
You're making us a laughingstock.

819
00:33:40,270 --> 00:33:40,790
Well,

820
00:33:40,790 --> 00:33:42,510
they threw them away,
and I picked them up.

821
00:33:42,510 --> 00:33:43,920
Now they're ours.

822
00:33:44,160 --> 00:33:44,750
Besides,

823
00:33:44,960 --> 00:33:47,360
they're not torn. They're perfectly fine.

824
00:33:49,920 --> 00:33:50,510
Aihua.

825
00:33:51,470 --> 00:33:53,400
Say something. Be the judge.

826
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:55,280
If we take

827
00:33:55,320 --> 00:33:55,960
the Cao family's cast-offs,

828
00:33:55,960 --> 00:33:56,590
people will think

829
00:33:56,590 --> 00:33:57,720
we're beggars.

830
00:33:58,110 --> 00:33:58,510
I'm telling you,

831
00:33:58,510 --> 00:33:59,770
anyone can look down on us,

832
00:33:59,770 --> 00:34:01,350
but not the Cao family.

833
00:34:01,520 --> 00:34:02,000
Lower your voice.

834
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:03,200
Keep your voice down.

835
00:34:06,480 --> 00:34:07,030
Mom.

836
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:09,400
She's got a point.

837
00:34:09,590 --> 00:34:10,670
What bullshit point!

838
00:34:10,670 --> 00:34:11,330
What point?

839
00:34:12,010 --> 00:34:12,880
You've just had it too easy.

840
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:13,730
You don't appreciate

841
00:34:13,730 --> 00:34:14,659
what you've got.

842
00:34:15,070 --> 00:34:16,070
Back in our day,

843
00:34:16,330 --> 00:34:17,760
forget picking up clothes to wear,

844
00:34:17,760 --> 00:34:19,070
we were eating tree bark

845
00:34:19,070 --> 00:34:20,440
and clay just to fill our bellies.

846
00:34:20,440 --> 00:34:21,050
Alright, alright.

847
00:34:21,050 --> 00:34:22,630
Now you get free clothes

848
00:34:22,670 --> 00:34:23,670
and you won't take them?

849
00:34:23,670 --> 00:34:24,320
Enough, please.

850
00:34:24,320 --> 00:34:25,920
Stop it, Mom. Please.

851
00:34:28,030 --> 00:34:28,510
Honey,

852
00:34:29,960 --> 00:34:31,290
my mom's got a point too.

853
00:34:32,030 --> 00:34:33,800
Mom, don't say anymore.

854
00:34:33,840 --> 00:34:34,300
Anyway,

855
00:34:34,440 --> 00:34:35,630
I won't wear these clothes.

856
00:34:35,630 --> 00:34:36,440
Aihua won't wear them.

857
00:34:36,440 --> 00:34:37,400
Qi Shi and Qi Zhi won't wear them,

858
00:34:37,400 --> 00:34:38,170
and no one in the family will wear them.

859
00:34:38,170 --> 00:34:39,900
You picked them up for nothing.

860
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:42,380
With the way you waste things,

861
00:34:42,380 --> 00:34:43,150
no matter how big the family fortune is,

862
00:34:43,150 --> 00:34:44,480
you'll burn through it.

863
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:45,550
I'm telling you,

864
00:34:45,550 --> 00:34:46,350
in this house,

865
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:47,440
my son is the boss!

866
00:34:48,070 --> 00:34:48,469
Aihua.

867
00:34:48,520 --> 00:34:50,330
Say something, will you?

868
00:34:58,920 --> 00:34:59,480
Honey.

869
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:02,930
It's just a few pieces of clothing.

870
00:35:03,180 --> 00:35:05,350
Maybe we can just keep them?

871
00:35:06,960 --> 00:35:08,220
You're such a good son.

872
00:35:09,120 --> 00:35:10,180
What are you doing?

873
00:35:10,730 --> 00:35:11,730
Get out of the way.

874
00:35:13,360 --> 00:35:14,190
Aihua, Aihua.

875
00:35:14,920 --> 00:35:15,800
Remember this.

876
00:35:15,960 --> 00:35:16,820
The worst thing

877
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:19,380
that can happen to a family
is a spendthrift.

878
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:20,120
This household

879
00:35:20,120 --> 00:35:21,190
still needs me to keep it running.

880
00:35:21,190 --> 00:35:22,030
Okay, Mom.

881
00:35:22,230 --> 00:35:23,150
You're the boss.

882
00:35:23,150 --> 00:35:24,590
Keep them if you want.

883
00:35:26,360 --> 00:35:26,960
Qinglian.

884
00:35:27,000 --> 00:35:27,700
Where are you going?

885
00:35:27,700 --> 00:35:28,830
Where are you going?

886
00:35:29,190 --> 00:35:29,790
Qinglian.

887
00:35:29,840 --> 00:35:30,960
Let her go if she wants to.

888
00:35:30,960 --> 00:35:32,620
Don't indulge her bad temper.

889
00:35:32,850 --> 00:35:33,670
Anyway, tomorrow,

890
00:35:33,670 --> 00:35:35,150
she'll come back on her own.

891
00:35:35,150 --> 00:35:35,680
Let's go.

892
00:35:35,920 --> 00:35:37,320
Time to eat. Wash your hands.

893
00:35:37,320 --> 00:35:38,380
Let's go, let's go.

894
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:40,330
Don't spoil her.

895
00:35:40,630 --> 00:35:42,030
Let her go if she wants to.

896
00:35:51,630 --> 00:35:52,030
Hello?

897
00:35:52,590 --> 00:35:53,000
Hello?

898
00:35:53,710 --> 00:35:54,190
Zhi.

899
00:35:54,570 --> 00:35:56,090
Mom ran away from home.

900
00:35:57,510 --> 00:35:58,440
Where did she go?

901
00:35:58,550 --> 00:35:59,440
I don't know.

902
00:36:00,070 --> 00:36:00,710
She said

903
00:36:00,960 --> 00:36:02,760
she won't come back

904
00:36:03,030 --> 00:36:04,290
until Grandma leaves.

905
00:36:04,480 --> 00:36:05,840
Come on, you should talk to Mom.

906
00:36:05,840 --> 00:36:07,190
Grandma is doing this for our own good.

907
00:36:07,190 --> 00:36:08,720
It's just some old clothes.

908
00:36:08,760 --> 00:36:09,670
You know how Mom feels

909
00:36:09,670 --> 00:36:11,000
about the Cao family.

910
00:36:11,280 --> 00:36:13,080
Those are Cao family cast-offs.

911
00:36:13,230 --> 00:36:15,030
How's that supposed to make Mom feel?

912
00:36:15,030 --> 00:36:16,370
Come on, they are only old clothes.

913
00:36:16,370 --> 00:36:17,880
No need to blow things out of proportion.

914
00:36:17,880 --> 00:36:19,000
You have no idea

915
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:20,960
how furious Mom was today.

916
00:36:21,320 --> 00:36:22,250
I'm telling you,

917
00:36:22,920 --> 00:36:24,580
don't say this in front of Mom.

918
00:36:24,710 --> 00:36:25,960
She'll definitely be unhappy.

919
00:36:25,960 --> 00:36:26,880
I'm just trying to keep

920
00:36:26,880 --> 00:36:28,190
this family together.

921
00:36:28,590 --> 00:36:29,110
Think about it.

922
00:36:29,110 --> 00:36:30,380
Grandma is already old.

923
00:36:30,380 --> 00:36:31,280
You can't change habits

924
00:36:31,280 --> 00:36:32,470
built over a lifetime.

925
00:36:32,470 --> 00:36:34,070
So you should persuade Mom

926
00:36:34,510 --> 00:36:36,400
to bear with it.

927
00:36:36,760 --> 00:36:38,490
Tell her not to let it get to her.

928
00:36:38,710 --> 00:36:40,110
If I try to talk to her now,

929
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:42,360
won't I just be walking right
into the line of fire?

930
00:36:42,360 --> 00:36:44,170
They're fighting their own battle.

931
00:36:44,170 --> 00:36:45,280
I'll end up being the bad guy

932
00:36:45,280 --> 00:36:46,190
no matter what I do.

933
00:36:46,190 --> 00:36:47,370
Why don't you go then?

934
00:36:47,370 --> 00:36:49,370
You're just over there talking big.

935
00:36:49,630 --> 00:36:51,110
I knew I couldn't count on you.

936
00:36:51,110 --> 00:36:52,710
I shouldn't have called you.

937
00:36:56,630 --> 00:36:57,630
This Qi Zhi.

938
00:36:58,550 --> 00:36:59,630
Ever since he went to
the provincial sports school,

939
00:36:59,630 --> 00:37:00,280
he's not on the same page

940
00:37:00,280 --> 00:37:01,360
as me anymore.

941
00:37:03,070 --> 00:37:03,630
When you come back,

942
00:37:03,630 --> 00:37:05,290
I'll have a good talk with you.

943
00:37:17,310 --> 00:37:18,740
I wonder if Mom's eaten anything

944
00:37:18,740 --> 00:37:19,650
out there.

945
00:37:21,190 --> 00:37:21,590
Dad,

946
00:37:22,360 --> 00:37:23,590
do something.

947
00:37:24,380 --> 00:37:25,940
What can I do?

948
00:37:27,810 --> 00:37:29,160
You know

949
00:37:29,190 --> 00:37:30,360
your mom's temper.

950
00:37:30,590 --> 00:37:33,120
Those two are at each other's
throats all day.

951
00:37:33,180 --> 00:37:34,620
Who can stop them?

952
00:37:40,280 --> 00:37:42,190
If Grandma doesn't leave,

953
00:37:43,400 --> 00:37:45,150
I'm afraid Mom won't come back.

954
00:37:45,280 --> 00:37:46,100
Actually, your grandma

955
00:37:46,100 --> 00:37:47,430
doesn't mean any harm.

956
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:49,110
Look at her.

957
00:37:49,920 --> 00:37:51,110
She's running herself

958
00:37:51,110 --> 00:37:52,240
ragged all day long.

959
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:53,030
She cooked all the dishes

960
00:37:53,030 --> 00:37:54,110
on this table.

961
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:56,880
We can't bite the hand that feeds us.

962
00:37:56,880 --> 00:37:57,980
How am I supposed to bring myself

963
00:37:57,980 --> 00:37:59,400
to tell your grandmother to go back?

964
00:37:59,400 --> 00:38:00,060
Then you...

965
00:38:01,110 --> 00:38:01,440
Here.

966
00:38:01,620 --> 00:38:02,070
Mom,

967
00:38:03,160 --> 00:38:04,000
take a rest.

968
00:38:04,710 --> 00:38:06,150
It's fine. You guys eat.

969
00:38:08,880 --> 00:38:09,510
Look.

970
00:38:09,880 --> 00:38:10,710
Your grandma

971
00:38:11,440 --> 00:38:13,300
collects garbage outside all day

972
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:14,700
and doesn't earn much,

973
00:38:14,920 --> 00:38:16,240
but she never keeps it for herself.

974
00:38:16,240 --> 00:38:18,070
She keeps bringing home baskets of fruit

975
00:38:18,070 --> 00:38:18,930
for the family.

976
00:38:19,480 --> 00:38:20,680
Let's put it this way.

977
00:38:21,080 --> 00:38:22,500
Since your grandma came,

978
00:38:22,550 --> 00:38:24,010
have you ever gone hungry?

979
00:38:24,280 --> 00:38:25,710
Have you ever washed dirty clothes?

980
00:38:25,710 --> 00:38:27,280
I don't want to come home

981
00:38:27,300 --> 00:38:29,100
exhausted from working all day,

982
00:38:29,360 --> 00:38:31,290
only to mop floors and wash dishes.

983
00:38:32,230 --> 00:38:33,400
Just think of your grandma

984
00:38:33,400 --> 00:38:35,360
as a bonus for our family.

985
00:38:36,100 --> 00:38:37,150
And your mom

986
00:38:37,180 --> 00:38:39,110
gets to rest at her parents' house.

987
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:41,840
Listen to yourself.

988
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:42,990
Would you dare say that

989
00:38:42,990 --> 00:38:43,790
to Mom's face?

990
00:38:44,800 --> 00:38:47,590
We are grateful Grandma tries her hardest.

991
00:38:48,190 --> 00:38:50,050
But it's still really tough on us.

992
00:38:50,590 --> 00:38:51,390
She forced...

993
00:38:51,960 --> 00:38:52,630
Look.

994
00:38:52,650 --> 00:38:54,480
She forced me to collect cardboard

995
00:38:54,480 --> 00:38:55,400
and bottles.

996
00:38:55,710 --> 00:38:56,830
Look at my hands.

997
00:38:57,800 --> 00:38:58,280
Look.

998
00:38:59,210 --> 00:39:00,280
If it weren't for Cao Xin,

999
00:39:00,280 --> 00:39:02,280
I would've crushed my fingernails.

1000
00:39:02,800 --> 00:39:04,710
My mom has a sharp tongue,

1001
00:39:04,960 --> 00:39:06,100
but she never forces us

1002
00:39:06,100 --> 00:39:07,350
to do everything.

1003
00:39:08,230 --> 00:39:09,630
Even when she punishes me,

1004
00:39:09,630 --> 00:39:10,590
it's because I did something wrong.

1005
00:39:10,590 --> 00:39:11,920
There's a reason for it.

1006
00:39:15,320 --> 00:39:15,960
I never thought

1007
00:39:15,960 --> 00:39:17,360
it would come to this.

1008
00:39:18,510 --> 00:39:19,440
I miss my mom.

1009
00:39:19,630 --> 00:39:21,280
You think I don't miss her too?

1010
00:39:21,280 --> 00:39:22,880
But you feel bad for your mom,

1011
00:39:23,230 --> 00:39:25,150
and I feel bad for mine too.

1012
00:39:25,400 --> 00:39:26,810
I can't just say

1013
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:28,530
we should kick Grandma out.

1014
00:39:28,710 --> 00:39:30,370
I can't bring myself to say it.

1015
00:39:32,440 --> 00:39:34,000
You know who's really stuck in the middle?

1016
00:39:34,000 --> 00:39:34,590
Me.

1017
00:39:34,840 --> 00:39:36,280
I've got it the hardest.

1018
00:39:40,320 --> 00:39:41,450
Whose house is this?

1019
00:39:41,550 --> 00:39:42,610
What is this smell?

1020
00:39:43,630 --> 00:39:44,160
Grandpa,

1021
00:39:45,150 --> 00:39:46,110
do you smell that?

1022
00:39:46,110 --> 00:39:47,070
I smell it.

1023
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:49,110
It's almost knocking me out.

1024
00:39:49,480 --> 00:39:50,730
It stinks.

1025
00:39:52,630 --> 00:39:54,360
That old lady from the Qi family

1026
00:39:54,400 --> 00:39:55,600
is quite a character.

1027
00:39:56,110 --> 00:39:57,000
She's a master.

1028
00:39:58,230 --> 00:40:00,070
Qinglian's tough as nails,

1029
00:40:00,400 --> 00:40:02,070
and she still got run off.

1030
00:40:04,040 --> 00:40:04,850
I guess

1031
00:40:04,880 --> 00:40:06,610
this smell has something to do with her.

1032
00:40:06,610 --> 00:40:07,610
What should we do?

1033
00:40:07,670 --> 00:40:09,110
We just have to put up with it?

1034
00:40:09,110 --> 00:40:10,150
Don't worry.

1035
00:40:10,550 --> 00:40:12,080
Someone will deal with her.

1036
00:40:12,770 --> 00:40:14,160
Just wait and see

1037
00:40:14,190 --> 00:40:15,250
how this plays out.

1038
00:40:16,510 --> 00:40:17,080
Come in.

1039
00:40:17,110 --> 00:40:18,070
Close the door.

1040
00:40:18,200 --> 00:40:19,190
I'm going out to read for a while.

1041
00:40:19,190 --> 00:40:20,590
It smells too bad inside.

1042
00:40:31,070 --> 00:40:33,230
Why does it stink so much?

1043
00:40:33,360 --> 00:40:34,320
What is this?

1044
00:40:37,870 --> 00:40:39,830
What is this smell?

1045
00:40:39,880 --> 00:40:41,140
It smells a bit like...

1046
00:40:41,230 --> 00:40:42,110
Well...

1047
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:43,550
It stinks.

1048
00:40:43,710 --> 00:40:45,070
Nonsense.

1049
00:40:45,280 --> 00:40:46,610
It doesn't stink at all.

1050
00:40:46,900 --> 00:40:47,770
This thing

1051
00:40:48,400 --> 00:40:50,550
smells bad but tastes good.

1052
00:40:51,110 --> 00:40:52,920
Your dad loves pickles.

1053
00:40:53,320 --> 00:40:55,070
The ones sold in town aren't authentic.

1054
00:40:55,070 --> 00:40:55,510
So,

1055
00:40:55,840 --> 00:40:57,960
I've been busy fermenting several crocks

1056
00:40:57,960 --> 00:40:59,290
to satisfy his craving.

1057
00:40:59,510 --> 00:41:00,150
Grandma,

1058
00:41:00,480 --> 00:41:02,100
our health textbook says

1059
00:41:02,200 --> 00:41:03,400
eating pickled food all the time

1060
00:41:03,400 --> 00:41:04,600
is bad for our health.

1061
00:41:04,760 --> 00:41:05,930
Nonsense.

1062
00:41:05,960 --> 00:41:07,690
I've eaten pickles all my life.

1063
00:41:08,030 --> 00:41:09,590
I don't feel anything wrong.

1064
00:41:09,590 --> 00:41:10,590
Don't listen to them.

1065
00:41:10,590 --> 00:41:11,320
Listen to me.

1066
00:41:13,550 --> 00:41:14,190
Mom,

1067
00:41:15,030 --> 00:41:16,830
how about you make a little less?

1068
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:17,760
We can't eat it all.

1069
00:41:17,760 --> 00:41:19,420
We really can't eat that much.

1070
00:41:19,430 --> 00:41:20,000
Besides,

1071
00:41:20,030 --> 00:41:21,630
this smell is too strong.

1072
00:41:21,710 --> 00:41:22,400
Right.

1073
00:41:22,550 --> 00:41:23,080
Grandma,

1074
00:41:23,160 --> 00:41:23,880
the neighbors

1075
00:41:23,880 --> 00:41:24,840
will complain.

1076
00:41:25,630 --> 00:41:26,560
That's perfect.

1077
00:41:26,740 --> 00:41:27,950
Then I'll make more.

1078
00:41:28,760 --> 00:41:30,150
I'll give some to everyone

1079
00:41:30,150 --> 00:41:31,920
except that Cao family.

1080
00:41:32,510 --> 00:41:33,510
Once they taste how good it is,

1081
00:41:33,510 --> 00:41:35,170
they won't complain any more.

1082
00:41:39,720 --> 00:41:41,190
Hard is the way, hard is the way.

1083
00:41:41,190 --> 00:41:42,590
So many forks, where do I stray?

1084
00:41:42,590 --> 00:41:44,280
A time will come to ride the wind
and cleave the waves.

1085
00:41:44,280 --> 00:41:46,410
Set sail straight across the vast sea.

1086
00:41:48,490 --> 00:41:49,840
A golden goblet of fine wine
costs ten thousand coins.

1087
00:41:49,840 --> 00:41:52,700
A jade plate of delicacies
worth ten thousand more.

1088
00:41:52,700 --> 00:41:53,760
I lay down my cup,
drop my chopsticks, cannot eat.

1089
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:56,420
Draw my sword, look all around,
my heart adrift.

1090
00:41:58,880 --> 00:42:00,140
Why are you out so late?

1091
00:42:00,150 --> 00:42:01,230
Why are you out?

1092
00:42:02,280 --> 00:42:03,280
You know why.

1093
00:42:04,510 --> 00:42:06,710
The smell from your house is too strong.

1094
00:42:07,080 --> 00:42:08,400
I never knew your grandma

1095
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:10,000
could have this much impact.

1096
00:42:10,440 --> 00:42:12,300
Your mom really can't handle her?

1097
00:42:13,550 --> 00:42:15,080
My mom was so upset she left.

1098
00:42:17,050 --> 00:42:18,110
It's not that we don't want to step in.

1099
00:42:18,110 --> 00:42:19,250
We really can't.

1100
00:42:19,450 --> 00:42:20,150
You know, my grandma

1101
00:42:20,150 --> 00:42:21,210
isn't a bad person.

1102
00:42:21,920 --> 00:42:22,960
Everything she does,

1103
00:42:22,960 --> 00:42:24,150
she does for us.

1104
00:42:25,270 --> 00:42:26,590
She just doesn't realize

1105
00:42:26,590 --> 00:42:27,800
that her way of living

1106
00:42:28,190 --> 00:42:30,090
is completely different from ours.

1107
00:42:30,090 --> 00:42:31,020
Living together

1108
00:42:31,510 --> 00:42:33,190
is just uncomfortable.

1109
00:42:33,670 --> 00:42:35,130
Just like my grandfather.

1110
00:42:35,670 --> 00:42:36,970
He used to insist on

1111
00:42:37,000 --> 00:42:38,060
eating leftovers,

1112
00:42:38,760 --> 00:42:40,480
and he'd never throw out expired food

1113
00:42:40,480 --> 00:42:41,400
because he hated wasting anything.

1114
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:43,170
Until he ended up in the hospital

1115
00:42:43,170 --> 00:42:45,430
and spent hundreds on gastroenteritis.

1116
00:42:45,440 --> 00:42:46,230
Then he realized

1117
00:42:46,230 --> 00:42:47,890
that sometimes being thrifty

1118
00:42:48,230 --> 00:42:49,890
is just another kind of waste.

1119
00:42:50,960 --> 00:42:52,320
Once your grandmother realizes

1120
00:42:52,320 --> 00:42:53,590
that she's causing

1121
00:42:53,590 --> 00:42:55,000
trouble for you,

1122
00:42:55,080 --> 00:42:56,410
she'll leave on her own.

1123
00:43:00,360 --> 00:43:02,070
You mean...
